@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il36-nouns`
IMPORT `il36-s1-definitions`
IMPORT `il36-s4-departure`
IMPORT `il36-s5-s6-commencement`
IMPORT `il36-s2-exemption`
IMPORT `il36-s3-entity`

-- The public questions of the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law, 5786-2026, and
-- the machinery that answers them at the readings of the forks.
--
-- THE POLICY (Meng, SHRUG, 2026-10-08).  Where the text is silent or ambiguous there is one named switch
-- per ambiguity (il36-nouns.l4, `The readings`), the default is to decline by name, every other reading
-- is kept by name and tested, and a default declines a question ONLY where the readings give that
-- question different answers.
--
-- HOW.  Each public question lists the forks its answer can depend on.  Where a switch among them is
-- declined, the question is answered under each of the switch's two concrete readings (and, recursively,
-- the other declined switches): if the answers agree that answer is given, and if they differ the
-- question refuses, naming the first fork whose readings split it.  A switch the question does not
-- depend on never matters, declined or not.
--
-- THE FORKS EACH QUESTION DEPENDS ON
--   the exempt amount, s 2:               F2, F3, F4, F5, F6, F9
--   the qualifying income of a year:      F2, F4
--   the share of 2026 and the ceiling:    F4, F5
--   the exempt business income, s 3:      F4, F7, F8, F9
--   s 4 applies to the person:            F9
-- (F3 enters the ceiling only for income received from a relative, so the ceiling question is asked of
-- income not received from a relative; the exempt-amount question includes it.)

§ `Answers`

§§ `The refusals by name`

-- One refusal per fork: the text does not decide, the readings differ for this question, and the switch
-- that would decide it.  Each message names the readings.
@ref NOTES.md, fork F2
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not decide whether income attributed under section 62A from a transparent corporation is qualifying income, and the readings differ for this question` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text does not decide whether income attributed under section 62A from a transparent corporation is qualifying income (the exception in the definition of qualifying income, section 1, may be read as an exception to the exclusion of income attributed from a transparent corporation, or as a further exclusion), and the readings give this question different answers; fork F2, switch 'the reading of the exception for income attributed under section 62A'"

@ref NOTES.md, fork F3
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not decide the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030, and the readings differ for this question` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text does not decide the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030 (section 2(b) replaces paragraphs (1) to (3) of section 2(a) with a ceiling of 140,000 shekels for 2026 to 2029 and leaves paragraph (4), 150,000 shekels for 2030, in place), and the readings give this question different answers; fork F3, switch 'the reading of the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030'"

@ref NOTES.md, fork F4
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not decide whether a person in an adaptation year elected under section 14(b)(1) of the Ordinance is an Israeli resident for this Law, and the readings differ for this question` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text does not decide whether a person in an adaptation year elected under section 14(b)(1) of the Ordinance is an Israeli resident for this Law (section 2(e) disapplies section 14(b)(1) only for finding the day the person became a resident), and the readings give this question different answers; fork F4, switch 'the reading of the adaptation year'"

@ref NOTES.md, fork F5
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not decide the unit of the period of residence in 2026, and the readings differ for this question` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text does not decide the unit of the period of residence in 2026 in section 2(d) (days or months), and the readings give this question different answers; fork F5, switch 'the reading of the unit of the period of residence in 2026'"

@ref NOTES.md, fork F6
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not decide whether the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026 is prorated, and the readings differ for this question` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text does not decide whether the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026 is the ceiling of section 2(a)(1) prorated under section 2(d) or as listed (section 2(d) prorates the ceilings 'על אף האמור בסעיפים קטנים (א) ו־(ב)' and does not mention subsection (c)), and the readings give this question different answers; fork F6, switch 'the reading of the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026'"

@ref NOTES.md, fork F7
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not decide whether section 3 exempts an entity's income produced when the individual was not an Israeli resident, and the readings differ for this question` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text does not decide whether section 3 exempts an entity's business income produced when the individual was not an Israeli resident (section 2(a) says 'בעת שהיו תושבי ישראל' and section 3 does not), and the readings give this question different answers; fork F7, switch 'the reading of the residence of the individual in section 3'"

@ref NOTES.md, fork F8
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not decide whether section 4 takes away the exemption of an entity under section 3, and the readings differ for this question` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text does not decide whether section 4, which says the provisions of the Law do not apply to an individual, takes away the exemption of an entity under section 3, and the readings give this question different answers; fork F8, switch 'the reading of section 4 and the exemption of an entity'"

@ref NOTES.md, fork F9
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not decide in which year section 4 counts the days in Israel, and the readings differ for this question` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text does not decide in which year section 4 counts the days in Israel ('באחת מאותן השנים': either 2028 or 2029, or the year the person ceased to be a resident), and the readings give this question different answers; fork F9, switch 'the reading of the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel'"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      `the fork` IS A `A fork`
GIVETH AN a
`the refusal for` `the fork` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fork`
    WHEN `fork F2, the exception for income attributed under section 62A`
    THEN `the text does not decide whether income attributed under section 62A from a transparent corporation is qualifying income, and the readings differ for this question`
    WHEN `fork F3, the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030`
    THEN `the text does not decide the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030, and the readings differ for this question`
    WHEN `fork F4, the adaptation year`
    THEN `the text does not decide whether a person in an adaptation year elected under section 14(b)(1) of the Ordinance is an Israeli resident for this Law, and the readings differ for this question`
    WHEN `fork F5, the unit of the period of residence in 2026`
    THEN `the text does not decide the unit of the period of residence in 2026, and the readings differ for this question`
    WHEN `fork F6, the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026`
    THEN `the text does not decide whether the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026 is prorated, and the readings differ for this question`
    WHEN `fork F7, the residence of the individual in section 3`
    THEN `the text does not decide whether section 3 exempts an entity's income produced when the individual was not an Israeli resident, and the readings differ for this question`
    WHEN `fork F8, section 4 and the exemption of an entity`
    THEN `the text does not decide whether section 4 takes away the exemption of an entity under section 3, and the readings differ for this question`
    WHEN `fork F9, the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`
    THEN `the text does not decide in which year section 4 counts the days in Israel, and the readings differ for this question`

§§ `The readings the model takes by default`

-- Every switch declined (Meng, SHRUG, 2026-10-08).
@ref NOTES.md, the fork register
GIVETH A `The readings`
`the readings this model takes where the text does not decide` MEANS
    `The readings` OF
        `a case that turns on the exception for income attributed under section 62A is declined`
      , `a case that turns on the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030 is declined`
      , `a case that turns on an elected adaptation year is declined`
      , `a case that turns on the unit of the period of residence in 2026 is declined`
      , `a case that turns on the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026 is declined`
      , `a case that turns on the residence of the individual in section 3 is declined`
      , `a case that turns on section 4 and the exemption of an entity is declined`
      , `a case that turns on the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel is declined`

§§ `Resolving declined readings`

-- The first of the listed forks whose switch is declined, if any.
GIVEN `the forks` IS A LIST OF `A fork`
      `the readings` IS A `The readings`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A fork`
`the first declined fork among` `the forks` `in` `the readings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the forks`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the head` FOLLOWED BY `the rest` THEN
        IF `the fork is declined` `the head`
        THEN JUST `the head`
        ELSE `the first declined fork among` `the rest` `in` `the readings`
    WHERE
        `the fork is declined` `the fork` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the fork`
            WHEN `fork F2, the exception for income attributed under section 62A`
            THEN `the readings`'s `the reading of the exception for income attributed under section 62A` EQUALS `a case that turns on the exception for income attributed under section 62A is declined`
            WHEN `fork F3, the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030`
            THEN `the readings`'s `the reading of the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030` EQUALS `a case that turns on the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030 is declined`
            WHEN `fork F4, the adaptation year`
            THEN `the readings`'s `the reading of the adaptation year` EQUALS `a case that turns on an elected adaptation year is declined`
            WHEN `fork F5, the unit of the period of residence in 2026`
            THEN `the readings`'s `the reading of the unit of the period of residence in 2026` EQUALS `a case that turns on the unit of the period of residence in 2026 is declined`
            WHEN `fork F6, the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026`
            THEN `the readings`'s `the reading of the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026` EQUALS `a case that turns on the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026 is declined`
            WHEN `fork F7, the residence of the individual in section 3`
            THEN `the readings`'s `the reading of the residence of the individual in section 3` EQUALS `a case that turns on the residence of the individual in section 3 is declined`
            WHEN `fork F8, section 4 and the exemption of an entity`
            THEN `the readings`'s `the reading of section 4 and the exemption of an entity` EQUALS `a case that turns on section 4 and the exemption of an entity is declined`
            WHEN `fork F9, the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`
            THEN `the readings`'s `the reading of the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel` EQUALS `a case that turns on the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel is declined`

-- The readings with one fork's switch set to its first (TRUE) or second (FALSE) concrete reading.  The
-- fields have eight different types, so a field in the wrong place is a type error, not a silent swap.
GIVEN `the fork`     IS A `A fork`
      `the first`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the readings` IS A `The readings`
GIVETH A `The readings`
`the readings with` `the fork` `set to its first reading` `the first` `in` `the readings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fork`
    WHEN `fork F2, the exception for income attributed under section 62A`
    THEN `The readings` OF
             (IF `the first` THEN `income attributed under section 62A is qualifying income although it comes from a transparent corporation` ELSE `income attributed under section 62A is not qualifying income because it comes from a transparent corporation`)
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the adaptation year`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the unit of the period of residence in 2026`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the residence of the individual in section 3`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of section 4 and the exemption of an entity`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`
    WHEN `fork F3, the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030`
    THEN `The readings` OF
             `the readings`'s `the reading of the exception for income attributed under section 62A`
           , (IF `the first` THEN `paragraph (4) is not replaced, so the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030 is that of paragraph (4)` ELSE `the ceiling of 140,000 shekels for income received from a relative also holds in 2030`)
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the adaptation year`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the unit of the period of residence in 2026`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the residence of the individual in section 3`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of section 4 and the exemption of an entity`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`
    WHEN `fork F4, the adaptation year`
    THEN `The readings` OF
             `the readings`'s `the reading of the exception for income attributed under section 62A`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030`
           , (IF `the first` THEN `a person in an elected adaptation year was not an Israeli resident while it lasted` ELSE `a person in an elected adaptation year was an Israeli resident for the purposes of the Law`)
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the unit of the period of residence in 2026`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the residence of the individual in section 3`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of section 4 and the exemption of an entity`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`
    WHEN `fork F5, the unit of the period of residence in 2026`
    THEN `The readings` OF
             `the readings`'s `the reading of the exception for income attributed under section 62A`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the adaptation year`
           , (IF `the first` THEN `the share of the 365 days of 2026 on which the person was an Israeli resident` ELSE `the share of the 12 months of 2026 in each of which the person was an Israeli resident on at least one day`)
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the residence of the individual in section 3`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of section 4 and the exemption of an entity`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`
    WHEN `fork F6, the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026`
    THEN `The readings` OF
             `the readings`'s `the reading of the exception for income attributed under section 62A`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the adaptation year`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the unit of the period of residence in 2026`
           , (IF `the first` THEN `the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026 is the ceiling of section 2(a)(1) prorated under section 2(d)` ELSE `the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026 is the ceiling of section 2(a)(1) as listed, 600,000 shekels`)
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the residence of the individual in section 3`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of section 4 and the exemption of an entity`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`
    WHEN `fork F7, the residence of the individual in section 3`
    THEN `The readings` OF
             `the readings`'s `the reading of the exception for income attributed under section 62A`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the adaptation year`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the unit of the period of residence in 2026`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026`
           , (IF `the first` THEN `an entity's business income is exempt only if produced while the individual was an Israeli resident` ELSE `an entity's business income is exempt whenever produced in tax years 2026 to 2030`)
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of section 4 and the exemption of an entity`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`
    WHEN `fork F8, section 4 and the exemption of an entity`
    THEN `The readings` OF
             `the readings`'s `the reading of the exception for income attributed under section 62A`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the adaptation year`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the unit of the period of residence in 2026`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the residence of the individual in section 3`
           , (IF `the first` THEN `section 4 also takes away the exemption of section 3 for an entity's income earned through the individual` ELSE `section 4 does not touch the exemption of section 3 for an entity's income`)
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`
    WHEN `fork F9, the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`
    THEN `The readings` OF
             `the readings`'s `the reading of the exception for income attributed under section 62A`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the adaptation year`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the unit of the period of residence in 2026`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of the residence of the individual in section 3`
           , `the readings`'s `the reading of section 4 and the exemption of an entity`
           , (IF `the first` THEN `section 4 counts the days in Israel in either 2028 or 2029, whichever year the person ceased to be a resident` ELSE `section 4 counts the days in Israel in the year in which the person ceased to be a resident`)

-- THE RESOLUTION.  `the leaf` is the question at concrete readings.  Where no switch among `the forks`
-- is declined it is asked once.  Otherwise it is asked at each concrete reading of the first declined
-- switch (the rest resolved the same way): agreeing answers are the answer; differing answers name the
-- fork.  LEFT carries the fork that splits the answer; RIGHT the answer.  The fork named is the first
-- in the list that surely splits: where one reading of the first declined switch leaves the answer
-- undecided (a LEFT) and the other gives one answer, that answer cannot agree with all of the undecided
-- ones, so the first declined switch itself splits; where both readings leave it undecided, a deeper
-- switch splits and is named.
GIVEN `the forks`    IS A LIST OF `A fork`
      `the leaf`     IS A FUNCTION FROM `The readings` TO NUMBER
      `the readings` IS A `The readings`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A fork` NUMBER
`the number answered at every reading of` `the forks` `that the switches leave open, by` `the leaf` `at` `the readings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the first declined fork among` `the forks` `in` `the readings`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN RIGHT (`the leaf` `the readings`)
    WHEN JUST `the fork` THEN
        CONSIDER `the answer at the first reading`
        WHEN LEFT `the splitting fork` THEN
            CONSIDER `the answer at the second reading`
            WHEN LEFT `another splitting fork` THEN LEFT `the splitting fork`
            WHEN RIGHT `the second answer` THEN LEFT `the fork`
        WHEN RIGHT `the first answer` THEN
            CONSIDER `the answer at the second reading`
            WHEN LEFT `the splitting fork` THEN LEFT `the fork`
            WHEN RIGHT `the second answer` THEN
                IF `the first answer` EQUALS `the second answer`
                THEN RIGHT `the first answer`
                ELSE LEFT `the fork`
        WHERE
            `the answer at the first reading` MEANS
                `the number answered at every reading of` `the forks` `that the switches leave open, by` `the leaf` `at` (`the readings with` `the fork` `set to its first reading` TRUE `in` `the readings`)
            `the answer at the second reading` MEANS
                `the number answered at every reading of` `the forks` `that the switches leave open, by` `the leaf` `at` (`the readings with` `the fork` `set to its first reading` FALSE `in` `the readings`)

-- The answer or the refusal.
GIVEN `the forks`    IS A LIST OF `A fork`
      `the leaf`     IS A FUNCTION FROM `The readings` TO NUMBER
      `the readings` IS A `The readings`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number answered, or refused by name, over` `the forks` `by` `the leaf` `at` `the readings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the number answered at every reading of` `the forks` `that the switches leave open, by` `the leaf` `at` `the readings`
    WHEN LEFT `the fork` THEN `the refusal for` `the fork`
    WHEN RIGHT `the answer` THEN `the answer`

§§ `The forks each question depends on`

GIVETH A LIST OF `A fork`
`the forks the exempt amount depends on` MEANS
    LIST `fork F2, the exception for income attributed under section 62A`
       , `fork F3, the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030`
       , `fork F4, the adaptation year`
       , `fork F5, the unit of the period of residence in 2026`
       , `fork F6, the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026`
       , `fork F9, the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`

GIVETH A LIST OF `A fork`
`the forks the qualifying income depends on` MEANS
    LIST `fork F2, the exception for income attributed under section 62A`
       , `fork F4, the adaptation year`

GIVETH A LIST OF `A fork`
`the forks the share of 2026 depends on` MEANS
    LIST `fork F4, the adaptation year`
       , `fork F5, the unit of the period of residence in 2026`

GIVETH A LIST OF `A fork`
`the forks the exempt business income of an entity depends on` MEANS
    LIST `fork F4, the adaptation year`
       , `fork F7, the residence of the individual in section 3`
       , `fork F8, section 4 and the exemption of an entity`
       , `fork F9, the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`

GIVETH A LIST OF `A fork`
`the forks section 4 depends on` MEANS
    LIST `fork F9, the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`

§§ `Section 2 — the questions`

-- Is the person one the exemption is for: an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident, or a
-- veteran returning resident who became one, from 5 November 2025 to the end of tax year 2026?  No
-- fork reaches this question.
@ref Encouragement of Aliyah and Return Law s 2(a), s 1 (transcription lines 11, 15, 18)
GIVEN `the person` IS AN `An individual`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is within section 2(a)` `the person` MEANS
    `s 2(a) — the person is an immigrant or a veteran returning resident who became an Israeli resident in the period` `the person`

-- THE EXEMPT AMOUNT of the person's qualifying income in a tax year, in new shekels.
@ref Encouragement of Aliyah and Return Law s 2(a) to (e), s 1, s 4, s 6 (transcription lines 10, 18-26, 33, 37); the fork register
GIVEN `the readings` IS A `The readings`
      `the person`   IS AN `An individual`
      `the items`    IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the exempt amount of the person's qualifying income, reading` `the readings` `:` `the person` `items` `the items` `in the tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    `the number answered, or refused by name, over` `the forks the exempt amount depends on` `by` `the leaf` `at` `the readings`
    WHERE
        `the leaf` `the concrete readings` MEANS
            `s 2 — the exempt amount of the person's qualifying income, at the readings` `the concrete readings` `:` `the person` `items` `the items` `in the tax year` `the tax year`

@ref Encouragement of Aliyah and Return Law s 2(a) to (e), s 1, s 4, s 6; the readings this model takes where the text does not decide
GIVEN `the person`   IS AN `An individual`
      `the items`    IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the exempt amount of the person's qualifying income` `the person` `items` `the items` `in the tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    `the exempt amount of the person's qualifying income, reading` `the readings this model takes where the text does not decide` `:` `the person` `items` `the items` `in the tax year` `the tax year`

-- The qualifying income of a tax year (both kinds), before any ceiling.
@ref Encouragement of Aliyah and Return Law s 1 "הכנסה מזכה", s 2(a) (transcription lines 10, 18)
GIVEN `the readings` IS A `The readings`
      `the person`   IS AN `An individual`
      `the items`    IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the qualifying income of the person, reading` `the readings` `:` `the person` `items` `the items` `in the tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    `the number answered, or refused by name, over` `the forks the qualifying income depends on` `by` `the leaf` `at` `the readings`
    WHERE
        `the leaf` `the concrete readings` MEANS
              `s 2(a) — the qualifying income not received from a relative, at the readings` `the concrete readings` `:` `the person` `items` `the items` `in the tax year` `the tax year`
            PLUS `s 2(b) — the qualifying income received from a relative, at the readings` `the concrete readings` `:` `the person` `items` `the items` `in the tax year` `the tax year`

@ref Encouragement of Aliyah and Return Law s 1 "הכנסה מזכה", s 2(a); the readings this model takes where the text does not decide
GIVEN `the person`   IS AN `An individual`
      `the items`    IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the qualifying income of the person` `the person` `items` `the items` `in the tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    `the qualifying income of the person, reading` `the readings this model takes where the text does not decide` `:` `the person` `items` `the items` `in the tax year` `the tax year`

-- The share of tax year 2026 for which the person was an Israeli resident (s 2(d)): the fraction by which
-- the ceilings of s 2(a)(1) and (b) are scaled in 2026.
@ref Encouragement of Aliyah and Return Law s 2(d) (transcription line 25)
GIVEN `the readings` IS A `The readings`
      `the person`   IS AN `An individual`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the share of tax year 2026 for which the person was an Israeli resident, reading` `the readings` `:` `the person` MEANS
    `the number answered, or refused by name, over` `the forks the share of 2026 depends on` `by` `the leaf` `at` `the readings`
    WHERE
        `the leaf` `the concrete readings` MEANS
            `s 2(d) — the share of tax year 2026 for which the person was an Israeli resident, at the readings` `the concrete readings` `:` `the person`

@ref Encouragement of Aliyah and Return Law s 2(d); the readings this model takes where the text does not decide
GIVEN `the person` IS AN `An individual`
